# GUI test simplifications

The desks of the agentTools tests differ from a fresh installation of their distribution in the ways listed here.
Each difference is a simplification: it removes something a person on that desk sees or does, so no test checks it.
This file is the one place that lists them, so that each one can be retracted later.
How each one is configured is in linuxVersion/installation.txt of AgentsCoordination.

Each entry says what the desk normally does, what the setup changes, what the tests can not see because of it, and what retracting it needs.

## GNOME notification banners are off

Desks: ubuntu_gnome (this machine), fedora_gnome, debian_gnome_x11.
Normally: when GNOME refuses a window's request to come to the front, it shows a banner "<name> is ready" over the top of the screen for a few seconds.
The banner takes the clicks meant for the windows under it.
The setup: notification banners are off (show-banners false).
The tests can not see: the banner after the manager asks to come to the front, and a click that the banner takes.
Retracting it: the actions after the manager asks to come to the front wait until the banner is gone, or click the banner, as a person does.

## GNOME desks start on the desktop

Desks: fedora_gnome, debian_gnome_x11.
Normally: GNOME shows the Overview after login.
The setup: the user extension startdesktop@pilotio hides the Overview once the shell has started.
The tests can not see: the desk right after login.
Retracting it: start() leaves the Overview first, on the GNOME desks.

## The tiling desks use Alt instead of Super

Desks: arch_sway, void_i3, omarchy_hyprland.
Normally: the key combinations of these desks use the Super key.
GNOME on this machine takes the Super key before the VM viewer passes it to a VM.
The setup: the combinations the tests use (open the app menu, close a window) are also bound to Alt.
The tests can not see: the Super combinations a person uses.
Retracting it: a way to send the Super key into a VM.

## The omarchy tray icon of the manager is pinned

Desk: omarchy_hyprland.
Normally: the bar keeps tray icons in a drawer.
The drawer opens while the pointer is over it, and closes when the pointer leaves it.
The setup: the icon of the manager is pinned to the bar, outside the drawer.
The tests can not see: opening the drawer to reach the icon of the manager.
Retracting it: an action that opens the drawer, answered fast enough to click the icon before the drawer closes.

## omarchy windows are opaque and have no animations

Desk: omarchy_hyprland.
Normally: windows are translucent, more so when they do not have the focus, and they move into place with an animation.
The setup: every window is opaque, and animations are off.
The tests can not see: what shows through a window, and a window before it reaches its place.
Screenshot comparisons of a translucent window depend on what is behind it, and on whether it has the focus.
Retracting it: needed when tests check Fearless GUIs that are translucent themselves.
